# Exercise: Reading Fixed Bytes
#
# `io.read-n` reads exactly n bytes from input.
#
# Stack effect: ( n -- String )
#
# This is useful for binary protocols or fixed-format data.
#
# Example:
#   4 io.read-n   # Read exactly 4 bytes
#
# Your task: Understand fixed-size reads.
#
# To see it in action, fire up the REPL and try a small read:
#
#   $ seqc repl
#   > 4 io.read-n io.write-line
#   helloworld
#   hell
#
# (The first 4 bytes are consumed by `io.read-n`; "oworld\n"
#  is left in the input buffer.)
#
# When done, delete the marker line below.

# I AM NOT DONE

: test-read-n ( -- )
    # Can't test without actual input
    true test.assert
;
